# Lens CTA frost (do not regress)

The centered home upload button (Lens) must stay **semi-transparent frosted glass** in the idle state.

## Source of truth
- CSS: `.lens-glass` / `.lens-glass-dragging` in `src/app/globals.css`
- Class wiring: `lensFaceClassName()` in `src/lib/lens-glass.ts`
- Home usage: `src/components/home-coverflow.tsx` must call `lensFaceClassName(...)`
- Build gate: `npm run audit:lens-frost` (runs on every `npm run build` / Vercel)

## Required look
- Idle: frosted glass via `lens-glass` (alpha ≤ 0.45)
- Photo state only: opaque white + `overflow-hidden` is OK
- Soft blue frame halo via `animate-budget-halo` stays

## Never do without an explicit user request
- Restore solid fills like `bg-white`, `from-neutral-50 to-white`, or heavy `bg-white/80+` underlays on the idle Lens
- Put `opacity` / fade entrance animations (`animate-rise`, `animate-rise-delay`) on any **ancestor** of the Lens frost
- Combine `overflow-hidden` with frost on the idle Lens face (Safari bug)
- Revert to an old “solid Lens checkpoint” when shipping unrelated marquee/asset updates
- Bypass or delete `audit:lens-frost`

## When editing marquees / jewelry / sunglasses / bags
Touch only the track props and slide lists. Do not edit `lens-glass.ts`, Lens face classNames, or frost CSS unless the task is specifically about the Lens.
